DESCRIPTION >
    History backfill for events_customer_property_coverage_hourly_mv (deployed with BACKFILL skip:
    the deploy-time populate over `events` exceeds Tinybird's per-query timeout). Fills the window
    before the MV's promote seam in bounded chunks on on-demand compute, driven by
    scripts/backfill_customer_property_coverage.sh. SQL mirrors
    events_customer_property_coverage_hourly_mv_pipe EXACTLY so backfilled rows match
    forward-materialized ones. Reads from `events`, writes only this rollup.

    Seam safety: AggregatingMergeTree sums states and does not dedup; the window is half-open
    [start_date, end_date). Keep every end_date <= the MV's promote hour so an hour is never
    counted by both the forward trigger and a copy.

NODE migrate
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        org_id,
        env,
        customer_id,
        coalesce(entity_id, '') as entity_id,
        event_name,
        kv.1 as property_key,
        toStartOfHour(timestamp) as hour,
        sumState(toUInt64(1)) as event_count
    FROM events
    ARRAY JOIN JSONExtractKeysAndValues(properties::String, 'String') as kv
    WHERE timestamp >= {{DateTime(start_date, '2026-06-01 00:00:00')}}
        AND timestamp < {{DateTime(end_date, '2026-06-01 01:00:00')}}
        AND kv.2 != ''
    GROUP BY org_id, env, customer_id, entity_id, event_name, property_key, hour

TYPE COPY
TARGET_DATASOURCE events_customer_property_coverage_hourly_mv
COPY_SCHEDULE @on-demand
COPY_MODE append
